      "side": 1,
      "message": "Instead of having a field per target (and similar for os/arch) what about something like:\n\ntype OSTarget int\n\nconst (\n\tOSTargetDefault OSTarget \u003d iota\n\tAndroid \n\tDarwin\n\tFuchsia\n\tLinux\n\tLinuxBionic\n\tWindows\n\t\n\tInvalidOSTarget\n)\n\ntype ArchTarget int \n\nconst (\n\tArchTargetDefault ArchTarget \u003d iota\n\tX86\n\tX86_64\n\tArm\n\tArm64\n\t\n\tInvalidArchTarget\n)\n\ntype labelTargetValues map[OSTarget]labelTargetValue\n\ntype labelArchValues map[Arch]Label\n\n\nfunc (attr *LabelAttribute) SetOsArchValueForTarget(os OSTarget, arch ArchTarget, value Label) {\n\tif !attr.validTarget(os,arch) {\n\t\tpanic(fmt.Errorf(\"no target for os %q and arch %q\", os, arch))\n\t}\n\tattr.TargetValues[os].ArchValues[arch] \u003d value\n}\n\nfunc validTarget(os OSTarget, arch ArchTarget) bool {\n\tif os \u003c OSTargetDefault || os \u003e\u003dInvalidOSTarget {\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\tif arch \u003c ArchTargetDefault || arch \u003e\u003d InvalidArchTarget {\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\t// The next nil checks could be done once in an init routine somewhere.\n\t// I wouldn\u0027t expect the performance cost to be too high, but I don\u0027t\n\t// know your workload.\n\tif attr.TargetValues \u003d\u003d nil {\n\t\tattr.TargetValues \u003d make(labelTargetValues)\n\t}\n\tif attr.TargetValues[os] \u003d\u003d nil {\n\t\tattr.TargetValues[os] \u003d make(labelArchValues)\n\t}\n\treturn true\n}\n\n\nYou can also make some helper functions to go from a string to the enum values for each entry.  \n\nAnd can do:\n\nfunc (a ArchTarget) String() {\n\tswitch a {\n\tcase ArchTargetDefault: return \"conditions_default\"\n\tcase X86: return \"x86\"\n\tcase X86_64: return \"x86_64\"\n\tcase Arm: return \"Arm\"\n\tcase Arm64: return \"Arm64\"\n\t}\n\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"unknown value %d\", a)\n}\n\nfor easy output.\n\nNames you\u0027ll likely want to tweak and adjust - I used existing type names to help link to existing code but if you like this approach we can find better names for this layout.\n\nWith this approach, adding a new arch type/os is updating the enum constant mapping functions.\n\nAnother advantage to this approach that I like is the boilerplate code is more obviously now in support functions rather than part of the main code path.  Reading this code understanding how \tif v \u003d attr.targetValuePtrs()[os]; v \u003d\u003d nil {\nworked tooke me some time.",
