      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looking at the StaticProperties and SharedProperties type, I\u0027m not sure why they\u0027re needed.\n\nIt feels like you can always just pass StaticOrSharedProperties everywhere instead. And the comment on that type didn\u0027t help me understand why it\u0027s needed.\n\nIf you really need the separate types, then do:\n\ntype StaticProperties struct {\n  static StaticOrSharedProperties\n}\n\nfunc (p StaticProperties) Properties() StaticOrSharedProperties {\n  return p.static\n}\n\ntype SharedProperties struct {\n  shared StaticOrSharedProperties\n}\n\nfunc (p SharredProperties) Properties() StaticOrSharedProperties {\n  return p.shared\n}\n\nThen in the code here you\u0027d have:\n\ntype propertyAccessor interface {\n  func Properties() StaticOrSharedProperties\n}\n\nfunc bp2buildParseStaticOrSharedProps(...) staticOrSharedAttributes {\n  var nonconf []propertyAccessor\n  if isStatic {\n    nonconf \u003d []propertyFetcher{lib.StaticProperties.GetProperties()}\n  } else {\n    nonconf \u003d []propertyFetcher{lib.SharedProperties.GetProperties()}\n  }\n  \n  attrs :\u003d staticOrSharedAttributes{}\n  extractor :\u003d func(_ interface{}, input interface{}, ctx ..., arch string) {\n    setStaticOrSharedAttributes(\u0026attrs, input.(propertyFetcher).GetProperties(), ctx, os, arch)\n  }    \n   \n  var template interface{}\n  if isStatic {\n    template \u003d \u0026StaticProperties{}\n  } else {\n    template \u003d \u0026SharedProperties{}\n  }\n  parsePropertySets(\u0026attrs, ctx, module, template, nonconf, extractor)\n  return attrs\n}\n\nYou can also modify the extractor to always capture the variable too:\ntype attributeExtractor func(input interface{}, ctx android.TopDownMutatorContext, os, arch string)\n\nfunc extractorForPrebuiltAttributes(attr *prebuiltAttributes) {\n\treturn func(input interface{}, ctx ..., os, arch string) {\n\t\tplp :\u003d props.(*prebuiltLinkerProperties)\n\n\t\tif len(plp.Srcs) \u003e 1 {\n\t\t\tvar suffix string\n\t// rest of function as existing prebuiltAttributesExtractor\n\nI\u0027m not 100% sure this is better, but given 1 out of 3 uses you\u0027re already doing this (here - you capture attrs instead of typecasting) I think it simplifies things.\n\nCasting the input is probably unavoidable since there are tons of different fields and such cared about.  But I think that\u0027s ok.",
